ersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.j2wsK6IsW5yMW1jW","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"o1KN4idXTMdjXR08","name":"Hanging Fruit","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":-100000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A hook melon is suspended from its parent tree by a long vine. While connected to its parent tree, the melon has fast healing 10 but is @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{Immobilized}. It can detach itself from its vine as a free action. A hook melon will also detach if moved more than 10 feet from its parent tree. Once detached, it cannot reattach itself.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"UmP0egqFz7SCaJrV","name":"Steer","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Reaction.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An attached creature attempts to attack the hook melon or use a move action;</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The hook melon disrupts the action and uses Steal Stride.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"oH0ddLV9LsHC54Bq","name":"Branch","type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"value":"","gm":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"y1w2b4103el3ct3my65t":{"damage":"2d8+4","damageType":"bludgeoning","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":15},"attackEffects":{"value":["attach"]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"sFl1TWXCQEvzgxuz","name":"Attach","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":-50000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>When a hook melon hits a Small or larger living creature with its branch Strike, roots trailing from its torso attach it to that creature as a free action. This is similar to grabbing the creature, but the hook melon moves with the creature rather than holding it in place. The hook melon is @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg]{Off-Guard} while attached, and its host is encumbered unless the host is Large or larger.</p>\n<p>A hook melon is capable of controlling a dead or @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious} creature it is attached to, though it is limited to simple actions with the move or manipulate traits. The hook melon can still use all its own abilities and attacks, though it can be attached to only one creature at a time.</p>\n<p>A creature can escape an attached hook melon with a DC 25 check to Escape. An adjacent creature can forcibly remove the hook melon from an ally with a @Check[type:athletics|dc:20|name:Force Open DC|traits:action:force-option|showDC:gm]{Athletics} check to Force Open, which deals [[/r 2d8[bleed]]] damage to the attached creature. Killing the melon also frees the attached creature.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"2n5zuWbNstiUPebB","name":"Steal Stride","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The hook melon is attached to a creature;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The hook melon controls the attached creature's nerves, forcing it to ambulate. It Strides using one of the attached creature's Speeds, moving both itself and the attached creature.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"action"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":1},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}}],"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"pf2e":{"lootable":false},"core":{}},"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":90,"temp":0,"max":90,"details":""},"ac":{"value":20,"details":"","base":20},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":10,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","label":"Climb","value":10}],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"bludgeoning","value":5},{"type":"fire","value":5}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["arboreal","fey"],"details":"(can't speak any language)"},"level":{"value":4},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Hook melons are a strange and unsettling breed of fruit that dangle from the branches of their parent tree by a vine growing from their \"neck.\" When fully ripe, they bear an uncanny resemblance to a headless humanoid body.</p>\n<p>While most fruit disperses a plant's seeds by enticing other creatures into eating them, hook melons take a different approach. When intertwined with another creature's nervous system, the root-like fibers that trail from their torso allow the hook melon a limited amount of control over a creature's movements. They use this control to travel as far as possible from their parent tree and seek out a suitable place to sprout, often bludgeoning their unwilling host into unconsciousness or death in the process.</p>\n<p>Hook melons possess a surprising degree of intelligence for a plant, considering the sophistication required to control another creature's body. Sometimes a group of hook melons (called a gallows) will cooperate to ambush larger groups of creatures, ensuring that at least one of their kind can escape while attached to a suitable host.</p>\n<p>Occasionally, a hook melon will shun its biological drive and forgo sprouting in favor of further exploration. Such individuals have been known to disguise themselves with shapeless clothing in order to pass through inhabited areas.</p>\n<p>Sightings of unusual centaur-like silhouettes lumbering across forests can sometimes be attributed to these macabre fruits.</p>\n<h2>Selective Hosting</h2>\n<p>Though clearly plant-based life forms, hook melons possess eerie intellects, and their personalities are as alien to most humanoids as their invertebrate anatomy. Most hook melons prefer to attach to deer, large birds, and other swift-moving forest creatures, but for whatever reason, some instead have a predilection for humanoid bodies.</p>\n<h2>Monster Part Subsystem</h2>\n<p><strong>Hook Melon Creature 4 </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 12/27/50 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Athletics)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, energy resistant (positive), evil, sensory (scent), strength, wild, wisdomd</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary","authors":"Nathan Ross","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":2},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":-1},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":-3}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":11,"senses":[{"type":"scent","acuity":"imprecise","range":60},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"precise","range":30}],"vision":false},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":8,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":13}},"traits":{"value":["evil","plant"],"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"med"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"prototypeToken":{"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"height":1,"width":1,"disposition":-1,"name":"Hook Melon","actorLink":false,"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"bar2":{"attribute":null},"randomImg":false,"light":{"alpha":0.25,"angle":360,"bright":0,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"speed":5,"intensity":5,"type":null,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"attenuation":0.5,"color":null,"negative":false,"priority":0},"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e/art/Tokens/hook_melon.webp","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"sight":{"angle":360,"enabled":false,"range":0,"brightness":1,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e/art/Subjects/hook_melon.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"6.1.0","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1663517316809,"modifiedTime":1729380603117,"lastModifiedBy":"ZdvNMqfYMlbFrAL2","compendiumSource":"Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e.pf2e-battlezoo-bestiary.Actor.Q9Tl6x9JK8WO2qjp","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}}